    "claim": "Store/dylib skew on pull-based deployments: cast_params converts URL params per the STORE record read at request time, while the generated execute wrapper is compiled into the FFI dylib at build time - pulling a commit that changes a command declaration (param types, params list) without rebuilding the crate panics on the mismatch (observed live 2026-08-11: camera snapshot params Integer->String, stale dylib wrapper get_int received DString(\"1920\") - a VALID value - and killed the handler thread on every poll). The store+generated-src commit is necessary but not sufficient: the deployed .so must follow. Recovery: (cd <crate> && cargo build --release --features=serde_support) - the watcher hot-reloads the fresh artifact. dev.github.update avoids the window entirely (ff-pull + rebuild_lib + unconditional FFI crate build in one step); recommend it over bare git pull for live instances.",
    "tags": "workflow,deployment,ffi,dylib,skew,cast-params,update",
    "source": {
      "doc": "owner panic report (Not an int: DString(1920)) + trace analysis, 2026-08-11"
    },
