    "claim": "Two session-ops lessons from the 2026-08-12 merge round: (1) git add -A in a repo a server instance ever ran inside sweeps runtime state into the commit - a stray newbound launched from repositories/camera wrote config.properties there and it rode a commit to the remote unnoticed (cleaned in camera ebdbeab, now gitignored); prefer explicit adds or check git status before add -A in store repos. (2) CCR container state can roll back to an earlier snapshot while the remotes keep everything pushed - local reflogs missing commits that ls-remote shows is the signature; recovery is fetch + fast-forward, and it is why push-early matters. Parallel sessions are live: hollis-session merged its kb deposits with this session mid-stream (newbound-agent c560da1); union merges of kb memory facets across sessions resolve cleanly when domains differ.",
